        {
          "id": "5ec3f152-da57-318e-95cc-f1948be3fd94",
          "content": {
            "id": "5ec3f152-da57-318e-95cc-f1948be3fd94",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Lufthansa throws hat in ring in bidding for TAP stake",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Germany's Lufthansa airline submitted a proposal on Thursday for a minority stake in Portugal's carrier TAP.</p><p>The company said it has formally filed its\u00a0interest with the government via state holding company Parpublica.</p><p>Rivals British Airways and Air France-KLM have also expressed interest in buying up TAP's planned sale of shares.</p><p>Portugal's government relaunched a long-delayed privatization plan for TAP in July, putting a 44.9% stake up for sale to an airline that could add scale and competitiveness.</p><p>An additional 5% is to be sold to TAP employees.</p><p>The government said last month it expects the planned sale of the combined stake to proceed smoothly.</p><p>Airlines interested in TAP must formally submit a \"manifestation of interest\" by November 21 and non-binding offers in the coming months.</p><p>Lufthansa said its aspirations as an investor took into account TAP's, quote,\u00a0 \"great strategic importance to the European aviation industry.\"</p></body></title>",
